# BLOCKING CONSTRAINTS — Read Before Anything Else

> These are not suggestions. Each was discovered through actual work in this phase.
> Acknowledge each one explicitly before proceeding.

- [ ] CONSTRAINT (for §4): `GET /api/skills` response shape is now `[]{id,name,version,status,error?,manifest}` (changed in §2 / commit `3265178`), NOT a bare `[]*skill.Manifest`. When §4 wires `SkillManagerMenu` to the LIVE endpoint, it MUST read the 7 schema fields nested under `item.manifest.*` (e.g. `item.manifest.description`), and MAY read `item.version` / `item.status`. Reading `item.description` directly will be `undefined`.

**Do not proceed until all boxes are checked.**

## Critical Anti-Patterns

| Pattern | Description | Severity | Prevention Mechanism |
|---------|-------------|----------|---------------------|
| Bundling pre-existing `STATE.md` / `config.json` drift into a feature commit | These carry unrelated drift (CRLF + `_auto_chain_active` GSD state + continuity tweaks). Mixing them pollutes the feature diff. | advisory | Stage only the feature's files explicitly (`git add <specific paths>`); never `git add -A` / `git add .` in Phase 5. |
| Trusting gopls "file is not in workspace" diagnostics | Advisory workspace noise on Go files. NOT real compile errors. | advisory | The real gate is `go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./...`. Ignore gopls "not in workspace" unless `go build` agrees. |
| Claiming a UAT issue fixed without flipping the tracking doc | Code fix + commit is not "done" until `05-UAT.md` (result + Gap status) and `05-REMAINING-WORK.md` are flipped. | advisory | Every §N closeout MUST update `05-UAT.md` Test + Gap, `05-REMAINING-WORK.md` §N→DONE, and `STATE.md`. |

